  "faq": {
   "title": "FAQ \u2014 Alex Carter, Creative Freelancer",
   "html": "<header class=\"bar\"><a href=\"/\">Alex Carter</a><nav><a href=\"/\">Work</a><a href=\"/services\">Services</a><a href=\"/faq\">FAQ</a><a href=\"mailto:hello@alexcarter.studio\">Contact</a></nav></header>\n<main><span class=\"k\">FAQ</span><h1>Questions, answered</h1>\n<p class=\"lede\">Common questions about working with an independent creative freelancer.</p>\n<details><summary>What kinds of projects do you take on?</summary><p>Branding, websites, photography, video, social content and motion \u2014 for small businesses, studios and agencies. If it is creative and digital, ask.</p></details><details><summary>How long does a project take?</summary><p>It depends on scope. A focused project usually takes a few weeks; larger ones are planned in phases with a clear timeline up front.</p></details><details><summary>How much does it cost?</summary><p>Every project is scoped individually. After a short call you get a written proposal with a fixed price.</p></details><details><summary>Where are you based?</summary><p>Replace this with your own location \u2014 and note that you work with clients remotely, anywhere.</p></details><details><summary>Do you work with agencies?</summary><p>Yes \u2014 agencies bring me in as a white-label creative for overflow and specialist work.</p></details></main>"
  },
